// ============================================================================
// Production 09 - EWI Activator Example 1 (Option 1: source = Gold_EarlyWarning())
// Indicator #2 Net Outflow - latest 30-min bucket per Scope, in bn (NetOutflow_Bn).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Primary Activator source: the newest 30-min bucket per Scope, exposing
// NetOutflow_Bn (billions). Set the alert threshold on NetOutflow_Bn directly in
// Activator. An OPTIONAL window x day-type tiered version (threshold datatable +
// Alert_Flag) is kept at the bottom for when window/day-type-specific thresholds
// are needed.
//
// Run in the DepositMovement KQL database; use the primary block as the source.
// ============================================================================

Gold_EarlyWarning()
//| where Scope == "TOTAL_BANK"                     // uncomment to scope to Total Bank only
| summarize arg_max(Bucket_Start, *) by Scope       // latest 30-min bucket per scope
| project Scope, Date_ICT, Bucket_Label, WindowCode, DayType, NetOutflow_Bn
| order by Scope asc

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ACTIVATOR SETUP (Option 1 - KQL Queryset -> Add alert -> open Activator item)
//   Object          : Scope  (TOTAL_BANK / RETAILS / NON_RETAILS - 3 objects)
//   Condition       : NetOutflow_Bn  ->  Numeric: is less than or equal to  <value>
//                     (e.g. -5.5 for -5.5 bn; more negative = worse outflow)
//   Tier (optional) : add L1/L2/L3 as three rules, each with a different <value>
//   Actions         : Email / Teams, with NetOutflow_Bn / WindowCode / DayType as
//                     dynamic content in the message
//   Evaluate every  : 30 minutes
//
// NOTE: a single numeric threshold does NOT vary by window/day type. For
// window x day-type-specific thresholds, use the OPTIONAL tiered block below.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------


// ============================================================================
// OPTIONAL - tiered by comparable-time window x day type (Total Bank).
// Emits an Alert_Flag (L0..L3) so ONE Activator rule can watch it (fire on
// 'Changes' + Alert_Flag != "L0_NORMAL"). Edit the datatable to retune.
// L1 = customer numbers; L2 / L3 from the Total Bank tab.
// ============================================================================
